    evidence: "documented",
    title: "The bone-rank system of Silla",
    text: "Silla society was divided by birth into bone ranks. The 'sacred bone' royal lineage, then the 'true bone' aristocracy, then head ranks six down to one. Rank fixed the highest office a man could hold, the size of his house, the colour of his clothes, the number of his horses and the utensils he could use, and people married within their rank. Able men of head-rank six, such as the scholar Choe Chi-won, found their way blocked and some went to study in Tang China instead. The hwarang, youth bands of aristocratic boys, trained in arms, poetry and Buddhist devotion.",
