    text: "Goryeo family life differed sharply from later Joseon. A newly married couple often lived for years in the wife's parents' house, the son-in-law working there, and children could grow up in their mother's home. Sons and daughters inherited equal shares of land and slaves, and a daughter could carry out ancestral rites. Widows remarried without stigma, and a woman kept control of her own property. Genealogies recorded daughters' lines as well as sons'. All this changed under Joseon's Confucian reforms, but slowly, over three centuries.",
