    title: "Village compacts, hyangyak",
    text: "Joseon Confucians such as Yi I (Yulgok) promoted hyangyak, village compacts modelled on the Song Lü family compact. Members pledged four things: to encourage each other in virtue, to correct each other's faults, to treat each other with propriety, and to help in disaster and hardship, such as fire, flood, illness, death and poverty. Meetings kept a register of good and bad deeds and could punish by public censure. In practice the compacts were run by local yangban and reinforced their authority over commoners, but they also organised mutual aid. Commoner villages had their own associations, gye, for funerals and festivals.",
