    text: "After annexation in 1910, the Japanese Government-General carried out a cadastral survey that registered land in individual ownership. Land that could not be documented, including much held by custom, passed to the colonial state or to Japanese companies such as the Oriental Development Company. Korean rice was then exported to Japan in huge quantities, while Korean rice consumption fell and farmers ate millet imported from Manchuria. By the 1930s most farmers were tenants paying half or more of their crop in rent, and hundreds of thousands left for Manchuria and Japan.",
